        "original_id": "49f4d6b5-7691-5917-b6a6-57ad21df1ec6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Roger Brian Morris\n- Projects: Channel Tunnel, hovertrain project\n- Places: Folkestone, Kent, Coquelles, Pas-de-Calais, Calais, northern France, English Channel, Strait of Dover, Eastern Europe, South America\n- Topics: railway engineering, rail systems\n\nFacts:\n- Roger Brian Morris was born on 19 March 1933 and died on 15 June 2001.\n- Roger Brian Morris was a pioneer in railway engineering.\n- Roger Brian Morris helped develop the rail system for the Channel Tunnel.\n- Roger Brian Morris also helped develop the hovertrain project and several railway systems in Eastern Europe and South America.\n- The Channel Tunnel is a 50.45 km rail tunnel.\n- The Channel Tunnel links Folkestone, Kent, in the United Kingdom, with Coquelles, Pas-de-Calais, near Calais in northern France.\n- The Channel Tunnel runs beneath the English Channel at the Strait of Dover and is also nicknamed the Chunnel.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
